Parallel input regression tests
===============================

Run from the build root, for each configured Lisp, for example:

  timeout 180 ./maxima-local --no-init --lisp=sbcl \
    --batch-string='run_testsuite(tests=[rtest_parallel_input,rtest_parallel,rtest_ask1]);'

Require the log to contain "No unexpected errors". A Lisp error can be
caught by Maxima's top level even when the process exits with status zero.
The complete `make check` suite includes these tests automatically.

rtest_parallel_input.mac loads parallel-input-check.lisp through the
normal test search path. Its 33 examples check the public parallel forms,
nesting, empty jobs, failure cleanup, known signs and integer properties,
ordinary serial questions, and exact integration on the serial path.
Concurrent integration still has shared database failures (issue #3); this
test does not certify its thread safety.

The helpers additionally check 12 input cases in each of the serial
fallback, calling runner, forced native worker, and public dispatcher.
They use separate STANDARD-INPUT and QUERY-IO streams and assert that
neither input was consumed and no question was printed. Native-worker
checks run only on a Lisp with supported threads. A private deterministic
LCG exercises 128 large signed integer inputs without changing Maxima's
random state. Ordinary READ and READONLY behavior is checked before and
after the failures.

The execution-site test creates a one-item job and explicitly runs it in
the caller or a joined native worker. It therefore does not rely on a
scheduler delay to prove that a worker exercised the refusal.
